From aa2238a4f9414c20692a12df52765532db4a6d53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek <liangjiajian@liangjiajiandeMacBook-Air.local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:27:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add a keyless car-machine broadcast forwarding entry

The extended build forced every start through AmapConfiguration.prepare, so a
phone without an AMap Key could not use the car-machine navigation broadcast at
all. This adds an independent entry that needs no Key: it reuses the existing
Amap Auto broadcast parser, NavigationSourceGate, Android LocationManager and the
NavAssist v3 UDP exporter, and never instantiates MapView, AMapNavi,
NavigationRepository or the SDK coordinate converter.

The exported session declares wgs84 because its only position source is Android
GPS. Every broadcast GCJ02 position field is removed before parsing, so a
broadcast fix can never be labelled as, or blended with, a WGS84 observation. A
fix keeps its receiver measurement time, so repeated exporter ticks cannot renew
a stale position, and mock, low-accuracy and out-of-range fixes are refused.

MainActivity now decides the startup route before any SDK initialization and
sends a keyless extended build to the new entry; AmapKeyActivity offers it too.
The embedded map still requires a Key. Stopping releases location, broadcast and
the exporter, and a restart builds a new session and exporter.

Assisted-by: DeepSeek
